# Common Rules

Framework-agnostic style + naming. Placement/layering: see `layering.mdc` and `decisions.mdc`.

## Naming

### Files & directories (manual — not ESLint)

| Type | Pattern | Notes |
|------|---------|-------|
| Nest controller / service / module | `auth.controller.ts`, `auth.service.ts`, `auth.module.ts` | Nest **dot.role** under `apps/api` (do **not** use JoyKit/Hono bare `route.ts` / `service.ts`) |
| Web feature / component | `sign-in-form.tsx` | kebab-case files; PascalCase component exports |
| Route entry (Next) | `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx` | framework-required names |
| shadcn UI | under `apps/web/components/ui/` | |
| Directories | `kebab-case` | Named by **domain/concern** (see `decisions.mdc`) |

### Identifiers (enforced by ESLint `@typescript-eslint/naming-convention`)

| Kind | Format |
|------|--------|
| Classes / interfaces / types / enums | `PascalCase` |
| Functions | `camelCase` or `PascalCase` (React components) |
| Variables | `camelCase`, `PascalCase`, or `UPPER_CASE` |
| Enum members | `PascalCase` or `UPPER_CASE` |
| Boolean vars (web only) | prefix `is` / `has` / `can` / `should` / `enable` |
| Leading `_` | Allowed for unused / intentionally ignored |

Prefer `as const` objects over TypeScript `enum`. Project-level constants used 2+ times: `SCREAMING_SNAKE` or a named `as const` object in the owning package.

## Style

- **Prettier** (root `prettier.config.js`) is the format authority: 2 spaces, single quotes, semicolons, trailing commas (`all`), printWidth 120
- Prefer `| null` over `undefined` for optionals; avoid `any` unless Nest/framework APIs force it
- Run `pnpm format` / `pnpm format:check`; do not fight Prettier with one-off style

## Imports (enforced by ESLint)

Order groups (blank line between groups), via `eslint-plugin-simple-import-sort`:

1. Side-effect imports
2. `node:` builtins
3. External packages (`@nestjs/…`, `react`, …)
4. Workspace packages (`@elynd/…`)
5. Path alias (`@/…`)
6. Relative imports (`./`, `../`)

Also enforced:

- `import type` / separate type imports (`@typescript-eslint/consistent-type-imports`)
- No import cycles (`import-x/no-cycle`)
- Package/layer boundaries (`eslint-plugin-boundaries`): web ↛ api/db; shared ↛ db/apps; db ↛ shared/apps; `api/common` ↛ `api/*` features
- Nest DI exception: see `backend.mdc` — constructor tokens must stay value imports (`@Inject(Token)`)

## Security baseline (always)

| Rule | Notes |
| ---- | ----- |
| No hardcoded secrets | env / secret manager only |
| No server secrets in client bundles | never ship `AUTH_SECRET` or similar into client code; session cookies are httpOnly |
| Validate external input at boundaries | Zod (or equivalent) at API/form edges |
| Parameterized DB access only | Drizzle / query builder — no string-built SQL |
| No production stack traces to clients | map via error filters/handlers |

## Quality

Smallest relevant set before claiming done (see also `invariants.mdc` DoD):

```bash
pnpm run lint
pnpm run format:check
pnpm run typecheck
pnpm run test
```
